# Load rules and JSON cells

The rules the loader applies to a line of ingested JSON before PostgreSQL sees
it, and the total reads of the JSON the coordinator itself asked PostgreSQL to
build.

PostgreSQL text cannot hold the character U+0000, and real atlas records do:
OCR of a scanned problem list left `\u0000` in a few statements. The loader writes
each such escape as `\ufffd`, the replacement character, so the statement keeps
its length and its reader sees where something was lost. The scan reads JSON
escapes in pairs, so an escaped backslash followed by the letters `u0000` is
left alone. A cell the coordinator built has the coordinator's own shape, so a
missing member there means zero, the empty text or false; input from the network
is never read that way.

## Note
The JSON text `line` with every escaped U+0000 written as an escaped U+FFFD.

## To withoutNul (line: Text) -> Text:
    If line contains "u0000" is equal to false:
        Return line.
    Let bs be text_bytes(line).
    Let n be length of bs.
    Let mutable out be a new Seq of Int.
    Let mutable i be 1.
    While i is at most n:
        Let b be item i of bs.
        If b is equal to 92 and i is less than n:
            Let mutable isNul be false.
            If i + 5 is at most n:
                Let zeros be item (i + 2) of bs is equal to 48 and item (i + 3) of bs is equal to 48 and item (i + 4) of bs is equal to 48.
                Set isNul to item (i + 1) of bs is equal to 117 and zeros and item (i + 5) of bs is equal to 48.
            If isNul:
                Repeat for c in text_bytes("\\ufffd"):
                    Push c to out.
                Set i to i + 6.
            Otherwise:
                Push b to out.
                Push item (i + 1) of bs to out.
                Set i to i + 2.
        Otherwise:
            Push b to out.
            Set i to i + 1.
    Return text_from_bytes(out).

## Note
Whether a file name is one of a directory's atlas record files: `records.jsonl`,
or a piece of a split release such as `records-0007.jsonl`.

## To isRecordFile (name: Text) -> Bool:
    Return startsWith(name, "records") and endsWith(name, ".jsonl") and (name contains "/") is equal to false.

## Test: load rules replace an escaped nul and nothing else

Expect that withoutNul("{{\"t\":\"a\\u0000b\"}}") is equal to "{{\"t\":\"a\\ufffdb\"}}".
Expect that withoutNul("{{\"t\":\"plain\"}}") is equal to "{{\"t\":\"plain\"}}".
Expect that withoutNul("{{\"t\":\"\\u0000\\u0000\"}}") is equal to "{{\"t\":\"\\ufffd\\ufffd\"}}".
Expect that jsonValid(withoutNul("{{\"t\":\"x\\u0000\"}}")) is equal to true.

## Test: load rules know the record files

Expect that isRecordFile("records.jsonl") is equal to true.
Expect that isRecordFile("records-0007.jsonl") is equal to true.
Expect that isRecordFile("problems.jsonl") is equal to false.

## Test: load rules leave an escaped backslash before u0000 alone

For all booleans escapedBackslash:
    Let mutable line be "{{\"t\":\"\\u0000\"}}".
    If escapedBackslash:
        Set line to "{{\"t\":\"\\\\u0000\"}}".
    Let out be withoutNul(line).
    Expect that (out is equal to line) is equal to escapedBackslash.
    Expect that jsonValid(out) is equal to true.

## To intOfJson (v: Json) -> Int:
    Inspect jsonInt(v):
        When Ok (n):
            Return n.
        When Err (e):
            Return 0.
    Return 0.

## To textOfJson (v: Json) -> Text:
    Inspect jsonString(v):
        When Ok (t):
            Return t.
        When Err (e):
            Return "".
    Return "".

## To boolOfJson (v: Json) -> Bool:
    Inspect jsonBool(v):
        When Ok (b):
            Return b.
        When Err (e):
            Return false.
    Return false.

## Test: json cells read what the coordinator built

Let v be jsonParse("{{\"n\": 7, \"t\": \"x\", \"b\": true}}").
Expect that intOfJson(jsonGet(v, "n")) is equal to 7.
Expect that textOfJson(jsonGet(v, "t")) is equal to "x".
Expect that boolOfJson(jsonGet(v, "b")) is equal to true.

## Test: json cells answer the empty value for a missing member

Let v be jsonParse("{{}}").
Expect that intOfJson(jsonGet(v, "n")) is equal to 0.
Expect that textOfJson(jsonGet(v, "t")) is equal to "".
Expect that intOfJson(jsonParse("\"7\"")) is equal to 0.

## Test: json cells read a boolean as it is

For all booleans b:
    Let mutable doc be "false".
    If b:
        Set doc to "true".
    Expect that boolOfJson(jsonParse(doc)) is equal to b.
